#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
prints — the prediction-market desk tool for scheduled economic prints.

Same machinery as bin/pm (frozen playbook, one frozen ticket per decision,
append-only ledger, calibration gate), pointed at Kalshi's strike ladders on
CPI, core CPI, CPI year-over-year, nonfarm payrolls, the unemployment rate and
weekly initial jobless claims. The client trades these on Robinhood; Robinhood
routes to Kalshi, so the ticker here is the contract there.

The model is a nowcast built only from public FRED series. Every model here is
deliberately simple enough to be graded: a trend, a regression on gasoline, an
autoregression on claims. The replay grades each one against decades of prints
and, where Kalshi has settled ladders, against the market's own price.

Nothing here places an order on any venue and nothing here holds a credential.

Subcommands
  prints calendar                          upcoming releases, market-implied vs model
  prints nowcast <PRINT>                   the model's distribution and its inputs
  prints ladder <EVENT_TICKER>             one event's strike ladder with model p per strike
  prints ticket <PRINT> [--event T]        frozen decision ticket for the nearest event
  prints record <ticket_id> --side yes|no --price P --contracts N [--replace]
  prints settle                            settle released events -> ledger, refresh gate
  prints calibrate                         calibration and gate from the live ledger
  prints replay <PRINT> [--periods N]      model-only calibration on FRED history
  prints replay-market <PRINT>             model vs Kalshi price on settled events (small n)
  prints playbook init [--prints CPI,CLAIMS] [--max-stake N]
  prints budget

Flags (before the subcommand): --no-capture, --quiet

PRINT is one of: CPI, CPICORE, CPIYOY, PAYROLLS, U3, CLAIMS
"""

import importlib.util
import json
